<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African money mkt shortage back above 9 bln rand.</title>
<headline>S.African money mkt shortage back above 9 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank said the South African money market shortage rose to 9.436 billion rand on Tuesday from 8.482 billion rand on Monday.</p>
<p>All of South Africa's &quot;big four&quot; banks had their three-month NCDs unchanged at 17.10 percent offered, while the 90-day BA rate was quoted steady in a 16.40 to 16.65 percent range.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
